{
  "id": "2026-10-02-suncatcher-orbit",
  "title": "Google just put four AI chips in orbit to see if they melt",
  "topic": "테크",
  "level": 3,
  "voice": "en-US-AvaMultilingualNeural",
  "sentences": [
    "Good morning!",
    "Yesterday a SpaceX rocket carried four of Google's AI chips into orbit.",
    "The satellite is a prototype for something Google calls Project Suncatcher.",
    "The idea is to stop building data centers out of concrete and grid power, and build them out of satellites instead.",
    "In low Earth orbit the sun almost never sets, so a solar panel up there can pull in up to eight times the power it would on the ground.",
    "The full design calls for clusters of eighty-one satellites flying within a kilometer of each other, talking over laser links.",
    "What went up yesterday is far smaller — four chips running on about one kilowatt.",
    "And it can only run them for fifteen minutes at a stretch.",
    "After that the chips shut down so the radiators can catch up, because there is no air in space to carry the heat away.",
    "The economics are a long way off, too.",
    "Google's own numbers say launch costs have to fall to roughly two hundred dollars a kilogram, which nobody expects before the mid-2030s.",
    "So this is not a product yet.",
    "It is a question being asked out loud: can you cool a chip, and keep it talking to eighty others, somewhere with no air and no repair crew?",
    "Try explaining that cooling problem out loud this morning — it is harder than it sounds."
  ],
  "summary_ko": [
    "구글이 어제 TPU 4개를 실은 시험 위성을 팰컨9 로 띄웠다 — 데이터센터를 콘크리트와 전력망이 아니라 위성과 태양광으로 짓겠다는 'Project Suncatcher' 의 첫 실물 시험이다.",
    "저궤도에서는 해가 거의 지지 않아 지상보다 최대 8배의 태양광을 받는다. 최종 설계는 위성 81개가 1km 반경 안에서 레이저로 통신하는 묶음이지만, 어제 올라간 건 1kW 짜리 하나다.",
    "진짜 벽은 열이다 — 공기가 없어 열을 못 버리니 칩을 15분 돌리고 식혀야 한다. 경제성도 발사비가 kg당 200달러까지 떨어져야 성립해서 2030년대 중반 이야기다."
  ],
